dogscoff wrote:
> Been playing a lot of tourists lately, after a few thousand dead
> wizards.
> I don't know why everyone complains about tourists being such a hard
> class- they start with lots of food, so you can play as slowly and
> cautiously as you like. You usually get tripe as well, so you can tame
> more pets. The camera is great for pacifist/racketering play, and the
> credit card & magic mapping scrolls are a bonus. Also, once I get a
> weapon up to skilled (usually short sword, but dagger if short swords
> are unavailable of saber if I can find one) I find them very effective
> fighters. Do tourists get much harder in the mid/ late game?

I think tourists only get easier.  They can #twoweapon, and they can get 
basic skill in just about everything (mine used Crysknives, which were lots 
of fun and interesting given that it's my only ascension so far that didn't 
use an artifact weapon)

The quest artifact is great fun, the quest nemesis is a cakewalk (at least 
for me.  He zapped a wand of sleep on his first turn, it was reflected and 
he never got another turn :)


Tourists are great!

>
> Anyway, my question is this:
> The Hawaian shirt doesn't actually seem to give any AC at the default
> +0 enchantment.

This is true.  Shirts are the same way.  Only useful once you've got them 
enchanted

> However it is a bit of a liability in shops, and
> although I'm sure it doesn't weigh much, it is just one more item to
> lug about. Is there any reason at all to wear it in the early game, or
> should I stuff it in a chest somewhere until I ID enchant armour?

Well, no one else has said this, but one possible reason to keep it is just 
because that's the way a Tourist Should Be Played.  I'd say it's a matter of 
style, if you don't want to wear the shirt, then stash it, there's no ingame 
reason to keep it until you can enchant it  (and there's always the chance 
of a polytrap runining it if you're wearing it).  For myself, I kept it just 
because it somehow didn't feel right to strip off a piece of armor and stash 
it, even if the armor does nothing for me :)


